    <md:content-id>m02517</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.11.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ccc80f79-cdb3-44ef-9fbb-a5079b5b49f5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will learn how to use the vertex form of a quadratic to determine the maximum or minimum value of a function and to solve problems.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>Find the maximum or minimum of a function by writing the quadratic expression that defines it in vertex form.</item>
  <item>Explain why the vertex is a maximum or minimum when given a quadratic function in vertex form.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities </emphasis>that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>9.11.1: Maximum and Minimum Value of a Function</item>
  <item>9.11.2: Does the Vertex Represent the Minimum or Maximum Value?
    <list>
      <item>9.11.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>9.11.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>9.11.3: Comparing Maximums between Quadratics
    <list>
      <item>9.11.3: Self Check</item>
      <item>9.11.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>9.11.4: Maximum, Minimum, and Analyzing the Vertex</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you'll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>9.11.5: Practice</item>
  <item>9.11.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
